{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{4x^2+3x}{2x-7}$ is a rational expression.\n\nTo find the derivative of rational expressions, we use **the quotient rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}\\right]\u0026=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)-u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{u'(x)v(x)-u(x)v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's differentiate!\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{4x^2+3x}{2x-7}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(2x-7)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(4x^2+3x)-(4x^2+3x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(2x-7)}{(2x-7)^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{The quotient rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(2x-7)(8x+3)-(4x^2+3x)(2)}{(2x-7)^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }(4x^2+3x)\\text{ \u0026 }(2x-7)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{16x^2+6x-56x-21-8x^2-6x}{(2x-7)^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{Expand}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{8x^2-56x-21}{(2x-7)^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{8x^2-56x-21}{(2x-7)^2}$, or any other equivalent form.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $y=\\dfrac{4x^2+3x}{2x-7}$.\n\n$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":"0","simplify":false,"value":"\\frac{8x^{2}-56x-21}{\\left(2x-7\\right)^{2}}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"static":false,"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
